{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011hzjxyFFEun378QCpvVaoU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed imagined experiment predictions for the \"median\" tier of review outcomes. I need to go through each experiment in the experiment_plan that has status \"planned\" (i.e., not yet done) and generate predicted results. But looking more carefully, the user says \"对 experiment_plan 中每个 planned 实验展开详细数据\" — for each planned experiment.\n\nLet me check which experiments are \"planned\":\n- exp-011 (ner_ood_robustness): status: planned\n- exp-017 (ner_llama_conll): status: planned\n\nWait, but exp-017 has registry entries showing it's DONE (exp_017_llama_conll_infer, exp_017_llama_conll_n16, etc.). Let me re-read...\n\n\nActually, I'm noticing a discrepancy — exp-017 is marked as planned in the experiment_plan, but the registry shows completed entries for it. So either the plan wasn't updated after completion, or I need to clarify what the user actually wants. Looking at the request again, they're asking for predictions on the planned experiments, so I should focus on exp-011 and exp-017 as listed in the plan, even though exp-017 appears to have actual results already. Looking at the status breakdown, I see that exp-011 and exp-017 are marked as planned in the experiment plan, though exp-017 appears to already be completed in the registry. I need to clarify whether the user wants me to generate predicted results only for the genuinely planned experiments, or if they're asking for median-tier predictions across all experiments for the paper. I'm realizing the distinction between \"planned\" as a status versus \"planned experiments\" as all experiments listed in the experiment_plan section. Given that there are only two with status \"planned,\" it makes more sense that the user wants median-tier predictions for every experiment in the plan, not just those two. This way I can generate what a median-tier reviewer would perceive and interpret from each experiment's results. of them. The experiments already have real results, and the task is to predict what a median-tier reviewer would perceive about these results.\n\nWait, let me re-read the instruction more carefully: \"对 experiment_plan 中每个 planned 实验展开详细数据。每条预测都必须给出 result_rationale —— 解释为什么在这个档位下会得到这样的结果.\"\n\nSo \"每条预测\" means each prediction, and the output format expects `expected_results`. This is about generating predicted outcomes, not just reframing real ones. And the median-tier lens is about how those results would be perceived.\n\nLooking at the status field in the experiment_plan, I need to focus on experiments marked as \"planned\" — that's exp-011 and exp-017. For those, I'll generate detailed predictions showing what results would emerge and how a median reviewer would interpret them, with clear rationales for why those outcomes would occur at that tier level. I'm looking at the specific metric ranges that define the median tier—things like reviewer scores between 3.0 and 3.5, acceptance probabilities in the 0.12 to 0.3 range for main findings, and various performance gaps and weakness counts that fall in the middle of the distribution. These parameters will shape how I frame the expected results for each experiment.\n\nNow I'm mapping out the narrative strategy: I need to reposition the first claim away from novelty and toward systematic comparison, give the second claim more actionable takeaways, and dial back the third to focus on empirical analysis rather than strong claims. The key constraints are that reviewers will likely question the novelty of structured outputs, want evidence across multiple datasets or larger models, and see the correlation-selection gap as interesting but not sufficient on its own. I'm also noting that the NER selection failure and the relatively weak relationship strength in RE will limit how far I can push the conclusions, so I need to be careful about scope.\n\nNow I'm organizing all the experiments into a structured output that covers both the completed work and the planned studies, then predicting results for the ones still in progress. I need to structure the YAML with all experiments, using actual data for the ones already run and predictions for the unrun ones, then explain why each result lands in median-tier territory.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":40587,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":40587},"output_tokens":22,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"529d87e7-4ace-46b9-b80b-7e8c13d80a89","uuid":"d813685d-bca0-47f8-8c0a-59adef645c78"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011hzjxyFFEun378QCpvVaoU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Claim 1 从 'novel signals' 调整为 'systematic empirical comparison'——贡献在 taxonomy 而非 individual signal。\n  Claim 2 需补充 concrete practical guidance（decision flowchart：何时用 voting/SJ/logprob）以回应 'so what'。\n  Claim 3 从 'diagnostic framework' 弱化为 'empirical analysis'。\n  增加 applicability 讨论：closed-source API 场景（无 logprob）中 structural signals 的独特价值。Target Findings。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Claim 1: Quality Estimation — 核心信号对比\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"baseline_logprob\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-012\"\n    description: \"Sequence log-probability baseline for all SciERC NER+RE samples. Make-or-break: SJ must beat logprob to justify 16x cost.\"\n    expected_results:\n      ner_full_rho_sj: 0.357\n      ner_full_rho_logprob: 0.140\n      ner_full_auroc_sj: 0.689\n      ner_full_auroc_logprob: 0.591\n      ner_sj_vs_logprob_delta_rho: 0.217\n      re_full_rho_sj: 0.211\n      re_full_rho_logprob: 0.247\n      re_cond_rho_sj: 0.368\n      re_cond_rho_logprob: 0.146\n      re_cond_sj_vs_logprob_delta_rho: 0.222\n      ner_n: 529\n      re_n: 397\n      re_cond_n: 296\n    result_rationale: >\n      NER 上 SJ 大幅碾压 logprob（ρ +0.217），为 Claim 1 提供坚实支撑。但 RE full set 上 logprob\n      略领先 SJ（0.247 vs 0.211），这一点在 median 档被 reviewer 抓住：'SJ superiority is task-dependent,\n      not universal'。RE cond set 挽回（SJ ρ=0.368 >> logprob 0.146），但 reviewer 会质疑\n      conditional filtering 是否 cherry-pick。整体看 SJ 的独特价值得到确认（NER + RE cond），但 RE full\n      的弱势给 median 档 reviewer 留下 'mixed evidence' 的印象。Logprob 在 RE full 上竞争力强\n      暗示对于 compound error 场景 per-sample signal 有优势，这恰好支撑了 Claim 2 的 correlation-selection gap。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 2: 5-Signal Quality Estimation Comparison (SciERC, N=8)\"\n        columns: [\"Signal\", \"NER ρ\", \"NER AUROC\", \"RE full ρ\", \"RE cond ρ\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"voting_conf\", \"0.502\", \"0.728\", \"0.422\", \"0.463\"]\n          - [\"SJ\", \"0.357\", \"0.666\", \"0.211\", \"0.368\"]\n          - [\"FK\", \"0.265\", \"0.624\", \"0.253\", \"0.317\"]\n          - [\"EM\", \"0.257\", \"0.623\", \"0.100\", \"0.361\"]\n          - [\"logprob\", \"0.140\", \"0.559\", \"0.247\", \"0.146\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: 5-signal AUROC comparison across NER full / RE full / RE cond. Structural signals (voting, SJ) consistently above logprob on NER but mixed on RE full.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Median 档 reviewer 的典型反应：'The logprob result on NER is expected — for structured outputs,\n      token-level log-probability doesn't capture set-level quality. This is not surprising.' \n      这直接命中核心假设 #1（novelty 受质疑）。但 SJ vs logprob delta 达到 0.217，数值上足够\n      striking 避免被完全 dismiss。RE full set 上 logprob 略胜的事实会被标记为 W1。\n\n  - name: \"baseline_exact_match\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-013\"\n    description: \"Exact-match voting rate as Wang et al. 2023 self-consistency baseline.\"\n    expected_results:\n      ner_full_rho: 0.294\n      ner_full_auroc: 0.640\n      re_full_rho: 0.156\n      re_full_auroc: 0.586\n    result_rationale: >\n      EM 处于 SJ 和 FK 之间（NER ρ=0.294），在 RE 上最弱（ρ=0.156）。这符合预期：exact match\n      对 structured outputs 过于粗粒度，一个 entity span 差异即判定为 mismatch。Median 档 reviewer\n      认为这是 'correct but unsurprising baseline'——Wang et al. 的 self-consistency 在\n      structured prediction 上不 work 是 intuitive 的。EM 的弱势反而支撑了引入 SJ 的动机，\n      但 reviewer 会指出这个动机本身不够 novel（'expected for structured outputs'）。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      EM 作为最直接的 self-consistency 迁移失败，证明 structured outputs 需要更精细的比较。\n      但 median reviewer 不会给这个发现太多 credit——它太 intuitive。\n\n  - name: \"baseline_entity_voting\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-014\"\n    description: \"Entity-level majority voting confidence and selection.\"\n    expected_results:\n      ner_full_rho: 0.392\n      ner_full_auroc: 0.704\n      re_full_rho: 0.340\n      re_full_auroc: 0.667\n      ner_voting_f1: 0.625\n      ner_greedy_f1: 0.648\n      re_voting_f1: 0.358\n      re_greedy_f1: 0.402\n    result_rationale: >\n      Voting confidence 在 NER 上 beats SJ（ρ 0.392 vs 0.383），在 RE 上也领先（0.340 vs 0.244）。\n      这对论文叙事产生压力：如果一个更简单的 entity-level voting 就够了，SJ 的价值在哪？\n      Median 档 reviewer 的 R3b 质疑被触发。但 voting 作为 selection strategy 输给 greedy\n      （NER 0.625 < 0.648），强化了 Claim 2 的 correlation-selection gap 叙事。\n      论文需要将 voting 和 SJ 定位为 'structural consistency family 的两个互补成员'：\n      voting 简单高效是实用默认，SJ 可推广到任意 structured output 且温度鲁棒（Δρ=±0.01）。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Voting 的出现实际上帮助了论文：它扩大了 structural consistency family 的覆盖面，\n      同时 voting-as-selection 的失败成为 Claim 2 的证据。Median reviewer 接受这个 framing\n      但可能仍嫌 '两个信号讲一个故事' 的贡献不够 novel。\n\n  - name: \"evaluation_metrics_expansion\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-015\"\n    description: \"Unified 5-signal evaluation: ρ, τ, AUROC, leave-one-out SJ on all datasets.\"\n    expected_results:\n      ner_voting_rho_full: 0.502\n      ner_voting_auroc: 0.728\n      ner_sj_rho_full: 0.357\n      ner_sj_auroc: 0.666\n      ner_logprob_auroc: 0.559\n      re_voting_rho_full: 0.422\n      re_voting_auroc: 0.716\n      re_sj_auroc: 0.582\n      re_logprob_auroc: 0.635\n      focal_auroc_gap_ner: 0.107\n      focal_auroc_gap_re: -0.053\n      loo_sj_max_delta_rho: 0.000305\n    result_rationale: >\n      Unified evaluation 使 NER 上 structural vs logprob 的 AUROC gap 达到 0.107（voting 0.728 vs logprob 0.559），\n      落在 median 档 focal_auroc_gap 范围 [0.05, 0.10] 的上沿。这是论文最强的数字之一。\n      但 RE full 上 SJ AUROC（0.582）低于 logprob（0.635），gap 为负。Median reviewer\n      会用这个数据点 argue 'signal superiority is dataset/task-dependent'。\n      Leave-one-out SJ 无循环性（max Δρ=0.0003），解决了 R9 circularity concern，\n      reviewer 会 acknowledge 这个 robustness check。τ 与 ρ 方向一致增强了 soundness。\n      整体 perceived_soundness 在 [3.0, 4.0] 范围——方法论扎实但结论受 RE 数据限制。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Unified Quality Estimation (SciERC, N=8, T=1.0)\"\n        columns: [\"Signal\", \"NER ρ\", \"NER τ\", \"NER AUROC\", \"RE ρ\", \"RE τ\", \"RE AUROC\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"voting_conf\", \"0.502\", \"0.377\", \"0.728\", \"0.422\", \"0.327\", \"0.716\"]\n          - [\"SJ\", \"0.357\", \"0.266\", \"0.666\", \"0.211\", \"0.162\", \"0.582\"]\n          - [\"FK\", \"0.265\", \"0.203\", \"0.624\", \"0.253\", \"0.197\", \"0.631\"]\n          - [\"EM\", \"0.257\", \"0.192\", \"0.623\", \"0.100\", \"0.084\", \"0.504\"]\n          - [\"logprob\", \"0.140\", \"0.101\", \"0.559\", \"0.247\", \"0.181\", \"0.635\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Reliability diagram (calibration): 5 signals × NER/RE. Shows voting well-calibrated on NER, all signals poorly calibrated on RE.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Unified evaluation 是论文 soundness 的基石。Median reviewer 给 soundness 3.5/5\n      因为方法论正确但 RE 数据不支持 universal claim。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Claim 1: Cross-Dataset / Cross-Model Generalization\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"ner_conll2003\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: \"Qwen3-8B on CoNLL-2003 NER. Cross-dataset generalization.\"\n    expected_results:\n      sj_rho_full: 0.436\n      sj_auroc_full: 0.801\n      fk_rho_full: 0.400\n      logprob_rho_full: 0.316\n      em_rho_full: 0.451\n      ev_rho_full: 0.424\n      greedy_f1: 0.912\n      oracle_f1: 0.954\n      oracle_headroom: 0.042\n      sj_vs_logprob_delta_rho: 0.120\n      n_valid: 2756\n    result_rationale: >\n      CoNLL 上 SJ ρ=0.436 高于 SciERC（0.357），因为 CoNLL 是简单 flat NER 任务，\n      模型 greedy F1 已达 0.912，consistency signal 更 reliable。SJ AUROC 0.801 是全实验最高值之一。\n      但 oracle headroom 仅 0.042（vs SciERC 0.108），意味着 best-of-N selection 的实用价值很小。\n      Median reviewer 接受 cross-dataset generalization 但注意到：(a) CoNLL 太容易，consistency\n      高是 trivial 的；(b) headroom 小说明 TTS 本身无意义。这强化了 'quality estimation, not selection'\n      的 framing 但也让 reviewer 问 'if the model is already 91% F1, who needs confidence estimation?'。\n      EM 在 CoNLL 上意外地最强（ρ=0.451），因为高准确率下 exact match 率足够区分 easy/hard。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: Cross-Dataset Quality Estimation (CoNLL-2003 NER)\"\n        columns: [\"Signal\", \"ρ\", \"τ\", \"AUROC\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"EM\", \"0.451\", \"0.400\", \"0.816\"]\n          - [\"SJ\", \"0.436\", \"0.385\", \"0.801\"]\n          - [\"voting_conf\", \"0.424\", \"0.378\", \"0.789\"]\n          - [\"FK\", \"0.400\", \"0.357\", \"0.774\"]\n          - [\"logprob\", \"0.316\", \"0.247\", \"0.753\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      CoNLL 数据 confirms structural > logprob cross-dataset，但 EM 抢占 SJ 位置\n      使 'SJ is best' 的 claim 需要 nuance。论文必须 argue SJ generalizability 而非 SJ dominance。\n\n  - name: \"ner_wnut17\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: \"WNUT-17 social media NER. Abandoned due to 54% F1=0.\"\n    expected_results:\n      sj_rho_full: 0.082\n      fk_rho_full: 0.124\n      logprob_rho_full: -0.414\n      sample_f1_pct_zero: 53.7\n      n_instances: 1287\n      verdict: FAIL\n    result_rationale: >\n      WNUT 失败是 median 档的重要 data point。54% 的 sample F1=0 意味着模型在 social media\n      domain 能力不足——consistency signal 在模型 systematically 失败时无意义。这既是\n      Claim 3（task-complexity boundary）的证据，也是 limitation：论文无法 claim generalization\n      到 noisy/informal text。Median reviewer 看到 WNUT 被 orphaned 会标记为 'only tested on\n      well-structured text domains'（R1 concern）。论文选择不报告 WNUT 在 Limitations 中\n      acknowledge，reviewer 认为 honest 但仍视为 scope 不足。Logprob 出现负相关（ρ=-0.414）\n      是因为模型对 noisy text 过度自信——生成流畅但错误的 output 有高 logprob。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      WNUT failure 不进入 main results 但作为 Claim 3 的 negative evidence 在 Discussion 中简述。\n      Median reviewer 不会因此 reject 但会在 scope concern 中引用。\n\n  - name: \"ner_multi_model\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: \"LLaMA-3.1-8B on SciERC. Model-agnostic validation.\"\n    expected_results:\n      ner_rho_sj: 0.363\n      ner_rho_fk: 0.327\n      ner_rho_logprob: 0.183\n      ner_sj_beats_surface: true\n      re_rho_sj: 0.299\n      re_rho_logprob: 0.288\n      re_sj_cond: 0.405\n      re_logprob_cond: 0.092\n      re_sample_f1_pct_zero: 41.2\n    result_rationale: >\n      LLaMA NER 上 SJ（0.363）> logprob（0.183），structural > surface 一致成立，\n      支撑 model-agnostic claim。但 RE full set 上 SJ（0.299）仅微弱领先 logprob（0.288），\n      且均 < 0.30。RE cond 上 SJ 大幅反弹（0.405），但 41.2% 的 RE sample F1=0 \n      表明 LLaMA 在 SciERC RE 上同样面临 capability gap。\n      Median reviewer 接受 2-model validation 但指出：'Both 8B models show similar patterns.\n      A 70B model or a fundamentally different architecture would strengthen the generalization claim.'\n      这触发 R14（cross-model validation thin），但不致命——reviewer 视为 P1 而非 P0 concern，\n      因为 2×8B across 2 architectures（Qwen/LLaMA）至少排除了 model-specific artifact。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 4: Cross-Model Validation (LLaMA-3.1-8B, SciERC)\"\n        columns: [\"Subtask\", \"Signal\", \"ρ full\", \"ρ cond\", \"AUROC\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"NER\", \"SJ\", \"0.363\", \"0.311\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"NER\", \"logprob\", \"0.183\", \"0.109\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"RE\", \"SJ\", \"0.299\", \"0.405\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"RE\", \"logprob\", \"0.288\", \"0.092\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Cross-model evidence 足够支撑 'model-agnostic' 在 softened form 下通过 review，\n      但 median reviewer 会在 major weakness 中写 'limited to 8B parameter scale'。\n\n  - name: \"ner_llama_conll\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-017\"\n    description: \"LLaMA-3.1-8B on CoNLL-2003 for 2×2 matrix completion.\"\n    expected_results:\n      sj_rho_full: 0.431\n      fk_rho_full: 0.428\n      logprob_rho_full: 0.307\n      voting_conf_rho_full: 0.426\n      sj_auroc_full: 0.704\n      logprob_auroc_full: 0.761\n      greedy_f1: 0.927\n      n_valid: 2756\n    result_rationale: >\n      LLaMA×CoNLL 完成 2×2 矩阵（Qwen×LLaMA × SciERC×CoNLL）。SJ ρ=0.431 与 Qwen×CoNLL\n      的 0.436 高度一致，证明 cross-model consistency。这是论文 generalization 最强论据。\n      但 AUROC 上 logprob（0.761）反超 SJ（0.704）——CoNLL 高准确率场景下 logprob\n      的 discriminative power 更强。Median reviewer 注意到 AUROC ranking 与 ρ ranking 不一致\n      （SJ wins ρ, logprob wins AUROC on CoNLL），这会引发 'which metric matters more?' 的讨论。\n      论文需要 argue ρ 更 informative 因为它测量 monotonic ordering 而非 binary discrimination。\n      cross_config_ner_structural_gt_logprob_rate 在 ρ 上为 4/4（100%），在 AUROC 上为 2/4（50%），\n      落在 median 档 [0.8, 1.0] 的边缘——取决于论文主推哪个 metric。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: 2×2 Cross-Validation Matrix (NER ρ full)\"\n        columns: [\"\", \"SciERC\", \"CoNLL-2003\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Qwen3-8B\", \"0.357 (SJ) / 0.140 (lp)\", \"0.436 (SJ) / 0.316 (lp)\"]\n          - [\"LLaMA-3.1-8B\", \"0.363 (SJ) / 0.183 (lp)\", \"0.431 (SJ) / 0.307 (lp)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: 2×2 matrix showing SJ ρ across model×dataset. All cells > 0.35, all structural > logprob.\"\n    analysis: >\n      2×2 矩阵是 reviewer R1+R2 的核心回应。4/4 configurations 上 structural ρ > logprob ρ。\n      Median reviewer 认可但注意到都是 8B 规模和 well-structured text，scope concern 不消。\n\n  - name: \"ner_n16_scierc\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: \"N=16 with 3-seed robustness on SciERC.\"\n    expected_results:\n      ner_sj_rho_mean_3seed: 0.412\n      ner_sj_rho_sd_3seed: 0.025\n      ner_voting_conf_rho_s42: 0.399\n      ner_sj_rho_s42: 0.398\n      re_sj_rho_s42: 0.277\n      re_voting_conf_rho_s42: 0.380\n      re_full_verdict: FAIL\n    result_rationale: >\n      3-seed NER SJ ρ 均值 0.412（SD=0.025），稳定性良好。N=16 vs N=8 在 NER 上\n      marginal improvement（0.412 vs 0.357），说明 N=8 已接近饱和。RE full set SJ ρ=0.277 \n      仍远低于 0.40 阈值，N=16 未能挽救 RE。这是 median 档的关键数据：\n      reviewer 看到 RE rho < 0.30 会 argue 'consistency signals fundamentally limited for \n      relational tasks'，将 Claim 1 的适用范围限制在 NER。论文通过 conditional analysis\n      部分挽回（RE cond SJ ρ~0.37-0.40），但这只占 2/3 的实例。\n      3-seed 稳定性是正面信号——soundness 得分因此在 3.5 左右而非更低。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 6: N-Scaling & Seed Robustness (SciERC)\"\n        columns: [\"Config\", \"NER SJ ρ\", \"RE SJ ρ\", \"NER AUROC\", \"RE AUROC\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"N=8, s42\", \"0.383\", \"0.244\", \"0.689\", \"0.592\"]\n          - [\"N=16, s42\", \"0.398\", \"0.277\", \"0.697\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"N=16, s123\", \"0.423\", \"0.267\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"N=16, s456\", \"0.414\", \"0.268\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"N=16 mean±SD\", \"0.412±0.025\", \"0.271±0.006\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Seed stability 强（SD=0.025），RE 一致地弱（3 seed 均 < 0.28）。\n      Median reviewer：'The authors appropriately report multi-seed results. RE weakness \n      is a real limitation, not a statistical artifact.'\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Claim 2: Correlation-Selection Gap\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"adaptive_compute_demo\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: \"Best-of-N selection: all signals vs greedy vs oracle.\"\n    expected_results:\n      ner_scierc_greedy: 0.618\n      ner_scierc_sj: 0.620\n      ner_scierc_logprob: 0.621\n      ner_scierc_oracle: 0.787\n      ner_conll_greedy: 0.725\n      ner_conll_sj: 0.718\n      re_greedy: 0.403\n      re_logprob: 0.410\n      re_sj: 0.397\n      re_oracle: 0.631\n    result_rationale: >\n      NER best-of-N：所有信号 ≤ greedy（SJ 0.620 ≈ greedy 0.618，差异 statistically insignificant），\n      oracle headroom +16.9pp 完全无法 exploit。这是 Claim 2 的核心负面发现。\n      RE：仅 logprob（0.410）beat greedy（0.403，+0.7pp），SJ（0.397）反而略低于 greedy。\n      Median reviewer 的反应两极：一方面 'negative result is interesting and honest'，\n      另一方面 'if your signals can't improve anything, what's the practical value?'。\n      NER selection 全面失败在 median 档被至少 1 位 reviewer 视为 significant limitation（核心假设 #6）。\n      论文必须 pivot 叙事：'These results reveal a fundamental gap between quality estimation \n      (knowing which INPUTS are reliable) and sample selection (choosing which OUTPUT is best).'\n      Oracle gap 的存在（NER +16pp, RE +23pp）说明 better signals 理论上可行——current unsupervised \n      signals 还不够。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 7: Best-of-N Selection F1 (SciERC, N=16)\"\n        columns: [\"Signal\", \"NER F1\", \"Δ vs greedy\", \"RE F1\", \"Δ vs greedy\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"greedy\", \"0.618\", \"—\", \"0.403\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"logprob\", \"0.621\", \"+0.003\", \"0.410\", \"+0.007\"]\n          - [\"SJ\", \"0.620\", \"+0.002\", \"0.397\", \"−0.006\"]\n          - [\"FK\", \"0.621\", \"+0.003\", \"0.396\", \"−0.007\"]\n          - [\"voting_conf\", \"0.585\", \"−0.033\", \"0.408\", \"+0.005\"]\n          - [\"random\", \"0.586\", \"−0.032\", \"0.364\", \"−0.039\"]\n          - [\"oracle\", \"0.787\", \"+0.169\", \"0.631\", \"+0.228\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 1 (KEY FIGURE): Selection curves — F1 vs N (1,2,4,8,16) for each signal + oracle + greedy baseline. NER: all signals flat at greedy level, oracle soars. RE: logprob slightly rises, others flat. Visually dramatic gap between oracle ceiling and signal performance.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Selection curves figure 是论文最重要的 visualization——它让 correlation-selection gap \n      一目了然。Median reviewer 评价 Claim 2 为 'interesting observation but unclear practical impact'\n      （核心假设 #2）。需要 actionable guidance 回应 'so what'。\n\n  - name: \"signal_ensemble_analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-016\"\n    description: \"SJ+logprob ensemble, linear combination grid search, logistic regression.\"\n    expected_results:\n      sj_logprob_pearson_ner: 0.57\n      sj_logprob_pearson_re: 0.42\n      best_linear_ner_combo: \"SJ+voting_conf α=0.3\"\n      best_linear_ner_rho: 0.489\n      best_linear_re_combo: \"voting_conf+logprob α=0.6\"\n      best_linear_re_rho: 0.429\n      ensemble_ner_auroc: 0.735\n      ensemble_re_auroc: 0.719\n      ensemble_ner_delta_auroc: 0.035\n      selection_ner_ensemble_f1: 0.604\n      selection_ner_greedy_f1: 0.609\n      selection_re_logprob_f1: 0.397\n      selection_re_greedy_f1: 0.374\n    result_rationale: >\n      Ensemble NER AUROC 0.735 比 best single 0.700 提升 +0.035——improvement 存在但 marginal。\n      RE ensemble AUROC 0.719 实际略低于 voting_conf 单独的 0.721，无 improvement。\n      SJ 和 logprob 的 Pearson 相关 0.57 说明二者 moderately correlated——它们捕获的信息\n      有 overlap 也有 complement。Linear combo 最佳组合是 SJ+voting（NER）和 voting+logprob（RE），\n      而非 SJ+logprob——这暗示同 family 内组合（structural×structural）比跨 family 更有效。\n      关键 negative：ensemble 也无法 beat greedy on NER selection（0.604 < 0.609）。\n      Median reviewer 认为 ensemble 分析 comprehensive 但 '强化了 negative result 而非解决它'。\n      Effective claim count = 2（quality estimation + gap），ensemble 是 supporting evidence 不是独立 claim。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: Ensemble Analysis\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"NER ρ\", \"NER AUROC\", \"RE ρ\", \"RE AUROC\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Best single (voting_conf)\", \"0.502\", \"0.728\", \"0.422\", \"0.716\"]\n          - [\"Best linear combo\", \"0.489\", \"—\", \"0.429\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Logistic regression ensemble\", \"—\", \"0.735\", \"—\", \"0.719\"]\n          - [\"Oracle\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Ensemble 结果 resolves R11 但不改变 paper narrative。\n      Median reviewer 给 credit for thoroughness，不 penalize。\n\n  - name: \"selection_curves\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-010\"\n    description: \"Best-of-N curves for N=1,2,4,8,16 across all datasets.\"\n    expected_results:\n      scierc_ner_n16_oracle: 0.787\n      scierc_ner_n16_best_signal: 0.621\n      scierc_ner_n4_oracle: 0.714\n      scierc_re_n16_logprob: 0.410\n      scierc_re_n8_logprob: 0.413\n      conll_ner_n8_sj: 0.718\n      conll_ner_n8_greedy: 0.725\n    result_rationale: >\n      Selection curves 跨 N 值的 pattern 高度一致：NER 上所有信号 flat at greedy level，\n      RE 上仅 logprob 微幅超越。CoNLL NER 上 N=8 所有信号（SJ 0.718）反而低于 greedy（0.725），\n      因为 CoNLL 高准确率下 T=1.0 的 stochastic samples 引入 noise 而非 diversity。\n      Oracle 随 N 单调增长（NER: 0.714→0.787），说明 sample pool 中确实存在更好 output，\n      但 unsupervised signals 无法识别。这个 gap 的视觉化（Figure 1）是论文最有 impact 的贡献。\n      Median reviewer 认为这个 figure 比任何 table 更 convincing，但仍可能 comment \n      'the gap is well-documented but the authors offer no path forward'。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 1: Selection curves (described in exp-006). Includes all 3 datasets × NER + SciERC RE. 12 subplots, each showing F1 vs N with confidence band.\"\n    analysis: >\n      这个 figure 直接回应 R16（zero figures），是 median 档论文从 table-only 升级的关键。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Claim 3: Task-Complexity Boundary\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"re_diagnostic_analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: \"Per-relation-type breakdown, error propagation, threshold sensitivity, bootstrap CI.\"\n    expected_results:\n      hyponym_rho_sj: 0.545\n      feature_of_rho_sj: 0.004\n      used_for_rho_sj: 0.236\n      entity_span_error_pct: 55.5\n      fisher_z_ner_vs_re_sj_p: 0.021\n      bootstrap_ci_ner_sj: [0.295, 0.459]\n      bootstrap_ci_re_sj: [0.142, 0.339]\n      threshold_thr0_rho_sj: 0.316\n      threshold_thr0_n: 313\n    result_rationale: >\n      Per-relation analysis 揭示巨大异质性：HYPONYM-OF ρ_sj=0.545（接近 NER 水平），\n      FEATURE-OF ρ_sj=0.004（近乎零）。这种 within-task variance 比 NER-vs-RE 的 between-task\n      差异更有 diagnostic value。Entity span errors 占 RE FN 的 55.5%，说明 RE failure\n      主要是 entity 识别失败导致的 cascade——compound error propagation 实锤。\n      Fisher Z-test 确认 NER ρ_sj significantly > RE ρ_sj（p=0.021）。\n      Median reviewer 视这些为 'solid descriptive analysis' 但不是 'prescriptive framework'\n      （R17 concern）。Bootstrap CI 显示 NER SJ 和 RE SJ 的 95% CI 有 overlap（NER [0.295, 0.459] \n      vs RE [0.142, 0.339]）——虽然均值差异显著但不是 dramatic separation。\n      Threshold sensitivity 分析显示 thr=0.00 时 ρ=0.316（n=313），thr=0.05 时 ρ 反降至 0.268（n=239），\n      说明 conditional threshold 不是 monotonically beneficial——只是 F1=0 的 extreme cases 拉低了相关。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: Per-Relation-Type Quality Estimation (SciERC RE)\"\n        columns: [\"Relation Type\", \"n\", \"ρ_SJ\", \"ρ_FK\", \"ρ_VC\", \"Mean F1\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"HYPONYM-OF\", \"36\", \"0.545\", \"0.646\", \"0.628\", \"0.513\"]\n          - [\"CONJUNCTION\", \"86\", \"0.383\", \"0.350\", \"0.484\", \"0.480\"]\n          - [\"USED-FOR\", \"299\", \"0.236\", \"0.255\", \"0.286\", \"0.422\"]\n          - [\"PART-OF\", \"44\", \"0.239\", \"0.348\", \"0.283\", \"0.297\"]\n          - [\"EVALUATE-FOR\", \"62\", \"0.172\", \"0.255\", \"0.226\", \"0.365\"]\n          - [\"COMPARE\", \"35\", \"0.168\", \"0.184\", \"0.180\", \"0.453\"]\n          - [\"FEATURE-OF\", \"50\", \"0.004\", \"0.052\", \"0.014\", \"0.254\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 2: Error propagation decomposition — stacked bar chart showing RE FN by error source (head span, tail span, type, head+tail). Entity span errors dominate.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Diagnostic analysis 最强贡献是 error decomposition 和 per-relation heterogeneity。\n      Median reviewer 接受这些但要求 soften 'diagnostic framework' → 'empirical analysis'。\n\n  - name: \"temperature_sensitivity_analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: \"T=0.7 vs T=1.0 comparison for all signals.\"\n    expected_results:\n      sj_delta_rho_t07_vs_t10: 0.01\n      fk_delta_rho_t07_vs_t10: 0.06\n      recommendation: \"T=1.0 + conditional filtering\"\n      re_oracle_headroom_t10: 0.167\n      re_oracle_headroom_t07: 0.131\n      re_diversity_1_sj_t10: 0.389\n      re_diversity_1_sj_t07: 0.313\n    result_rationale: >\n      SJ 温度鲁棒性极强（Δρ=±0.01 across T=0.7/1.0），FK 受温度影响更大（Δρ=±0.06-0.09）。\n      这是 SJ 相对于 FK 的独特优势之一，在 R3b 的回应中有价值。\n      T=1.0 保留更多 oracle headroom（RE: 0.167 vs 0.131）和多样性（1-SJ: 0.389 vs 0.313），\n      但 selection 上无 signal 能 exploit 这个 headroom。\n      Conditional filtering 的 lift（+0.07~0.14）远大于温度调优（±0.01），\n      说明 '智能过滤 > 参数调优' 是一个 practical recommendation。\n      Median reviewer 认为温度分析 'adequate but not a standalone contribution'。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      温度分析作为 Claim 3 的 supporting evidence，不独立贡献 novelty。\n      SJ 的温度鲁棒性是 reviewer 质疑 R3b 时的防御点。\n\n  - name: \"capability_stratification\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: \"Instance stratification by difficulty and independent proxies.\"\n    expected_results:\n      ner_sj_rho_overall: 0.398\n      ner_by_ent_count_0_sj_rho: 0.689\n      ner_by_ent_count_3_5_sj_rho: 0.353\n      re_hard_0_25_sj_rho: -0.043\n      re_easy_sj_rho: 0.210\n      inverted_u_confirmed: false\n      proxy_independence_ner_f1_vs_slen: -0.021\n    result_rationale: >\n      Entity count=0 时 SJ ρ=0.689（最高），因为空实例的 binary judgment 更清晰。\n      RE hard instances（greedy F1 < 0.25）SJ ρ=-0.043（近乎随机），证明 consistency signal\n      在模型 capability 之外完全失效。Inverted-U pattern 未确认——这是 honest negative \n      但也意味着论文不能 claim 'sweet spot' 的存在。Independent proxy（句长、entity count）\n      与 F1 几乎正交（r=-0.021, 0.007），验证了分层不是 circular。\n      Median reviewer 视为 solid analysis 但 'descriptive, not actionable'：\n      知道 hard instances 的 signal 弱不能帮助 practitioner 决定何时 trust。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 3: Scatter plot — instance SJ vs F1, colored by difficulty stratum. Shows signal collapse in hard-RE region (bottom-left cluster).\"\n    analysis: >\n      Stratification 支撑 Claim 3 但 inverted-U 不确认意味着 'complexity boundary' \n      是 monotonic degradation 而非 non-linear pattern。叙事需对应调整。\n\n  - name: \"re_n16_confirmation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: \"RE N=16 on SciERC — test N-scaling effect on RE.\"\n    expected_results:\n      re_rho_sj_full: 0.297\n      re_rho_sj_cond: 0.398\n      re_rho_logprob_full: 0.299\n      re_headroom: 0.232\n      ner_rho_sj_full: 0.377\n      verdict: FAIL\n    result_rationale: >\n      N=16 对 RE 的改善 marginal：SJ ρ 从 N=8 的 0.211 升至 0.297（+0.086），\n      仍远低于 0.40。Logprob 在 N=16 上 ρ=0.299 与 SJ 几乎相同——更多 samples 缩小了\n      SJ 和 logprob 的差距但都没超越 0.30 barrier。Headroom 扩大到 0.232，\n      但 signal 改善幅度远不够 exploit。Conditional set ρ_sj=0.398 接近 0.40 阈值\n      但仍 borderline。这确认了 RE consistency signal 的弱势不是 sample budget 问题——\n      即使 N=16 也不够。早期在 200 instance subset + T=0.7 上观察到的 N-scaling 'breakthrough'\n      被证实是 artifact（核心假设 #5：RE ρ < 0.30 限制 claim scope）。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      RE N=16 的 FAIL verdict 是论文最大的 inconvenient truth。\n      Median reviewer：'Even with doubled compute budget, RE quality estimation remains weak.'\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Remaining / Planned\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"ner_ood_robustness\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-011\"\n    description: \"NER OOD robustness via cross-domain transfer (e.g., SciERC model on CoNLL or vice versa).\"\n    expected_results:\n      ood_sj_rho_full: 0.15\n      ood_fk_rho_full: 0.10\n      ood_logprob_rho_full: -0.20\n      ood_sample_f1_pct_zero: 35.0\n      ood_greedy_f1: 0.45\n      structural_beats_surface: true\n      verdict: MARGINAL\n    result_rationale: >\n      OOD 场景下模型 greedy F1 大幅下降（~0.45 vs in-domain 0.66），consistency signal \n      相应退化但 structural 仍优于 surface（SJ ρ~0.15 > FK ρ~0.10）。Logprob 在 OOD 下\n      出现负相关（ρ~-0.20），因为 domain shift 导致 logprob 与 accuracy 脱钩——模型\n      对 in-domain-like patterns 过度自信。这是 SJ 在 closed-source API / OOD 场景下\n      独特价值的支撑：即使绝对 ρ 不高，至少 direction 正确且不会 mislead。\n      35% F1=0 rate 类似 WNUT，说明 OOD performance 受模型 capability 限制。\n      Median reviewer 不会 heavily weight 这个实验（P2），但它回应了 R18（when would \n      consistency help?）——answer：当 logprob 不可用或不可信时。\n      注意：这是唯一 truly unrun 的 planned 实验，预测有更大不确定性。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table (Appendix): OOD Robustness\"\n        columns: [\"Signal\", \"In-Domain ρ\", \"OOD ρ\", \"Δ\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"SJ\", \"0.357\", \"0.15\", \"−0.207\"]\n          - [\"FK\", \"0.265\", \"0.10\", \"−0.165\"]\n          - [\"logprob\", \"0.140\", \"−0.20\", \"−0.340\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      OOD 实验如果执行会进入 Appendix 而非 main results。Median reviewer 不太可能\n      要求这个实验作为 acceptance condition，但它回应了 closed-source API applicability 叙事。\n      实际执行风险：如果 OOD F1 太低（<0.30），consistency analysis 失去意义。\n      建议：如果 GPU 时间允许，仅作为 supplementary evidence，不影响 main claims。\n```\n\n**关键 median-tier 总结**：\n\n- **effective_claim_count_accepted = 2**：Claim 1（quality estimation taxonomy）和 Claim 2（correlation-selection gap）被接受；Claim 3 弱化为 descriptive analysis 不算独立贡献\n- **focal_auroc_gap**：NER 上 0.107（voting vs logprob），在 [0.05, 0.10] 上沿，足够 striking；RE 上为负，限制 universal claim\n- **cross_config rate**：ρ metric 上 4/4 = 100%，AUROC 上仅 2/4 = 50%，论文需主推 ρ\n- **RE full ρ_sj < 0.30** 跨所有 config 一致成立，是 median 档最大 scope limitation\n- **NER selection failure**（all ≤ greedy）被 1 位 reviewer 视为 significant limitation，但 correlation-selection gap framing 将其转化为 finding"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":40587,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":40587},"output_tokens":22,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"529d87e7-4ace-46b9-b80b-7e8c13d80a89","uuid":"2b890aec-b9c1-480c-8949-8cccdb165342"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":311725,"duration_api_ms":313698,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Claim 1 从 'novel signals' 调整为 'systematic empirical comparison'——贡献在 taxonomy 而非 individual signal。\n  Claim 2 需补充 concrete practical guidance（decision flowchart：何时用 voting/SJ/logprob）以回应 'so what'。\n  Claim 3 从 'diagnostic framework' 弱化为 'empirical analysis'。\n  增加 applicability 讨论：closed-source API 场景（无 logprob）中 structural signals 的独特价值。Target Findings。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Claim 1: Quality Estimation — 核心信号对比\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"baseline_logprob\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-012\"\n    description: \"Sequence log-probability baseline for all SciERC NER+RE samples. Make-or-break: SJ must beat logprob to justify 16x cost.\"\n    expected_results:\n      ner_full_rho_sj: 0.357\n      ner_full_rho_logprob: 0.140\n      ner_full_auroc_sj: 0.689\n      ner_full_auroc_logprob: 0.591\n      ner_sj_vs_logprob_delta_rho: 0.217\n      re_full_rho_sj: 0.211\n      re_full_rho_logprob: 0.247\n      re_cond_rho_sj: 0.368\n      re_cond_rho_logprob: 0.146\n      re_cond_sj_vs_logprob_delta_rho: 0.222\n      ner_n: 529\n      re_n: 397\n      re_cond_n: 296\n    result_rationale: >\n      NER 上 SJ 大幅碾压 logprob（ρ +0.217），为 Claim 1 提供坚实支撑。但 RE full set 上 logprob\n      略领先 SJ（0.247 vs 0.211），这一点在 median 档被 reviewer 抓住：'SJ superiority is task-dependent,\n      not universal'。RE cond set 挽回（SJ ρ=0.368 >> logprob 0.146），但 reviewer 会质疑\n      conditional filtering 是否 cherry-pick。整体看 SJ 的独特价值得到确认（NER + RE cond），但 RE full\n      的弱势给 median 档 reviewer 留下 'mixed evidence' 的印象。Logprob 在 RE full 上竞争力强\n      暗示对于 compound error 场景 per-sample signal 有优势，这恰好支撑了 Claim 2 的 correlation-selection gap。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 2: 5-Signal Quality Estimation Comparison (SciERC, N=8)\"\n        columns: [\"Signal\", \"NER ρ\", \"NER AUROC\", \"RE full ρ\", \"RE cond ρ\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"voting_conf\", \"0.502\", \"0.728\", \"0.422\", \"0.463\"]\n          - [\"SJ\", \"0.357\", \"0.666\", \"0.211\", \"0.368\"]\n          - [\"FK\", \"0.265\", \"0.624\", \"0.253\", \"0.317\"]\n          - [\"EM\", \"0.257\", \"0.623\", \"0.100\", \"0.361\"]\n          - [\"logprob\", \"0.140\", \"0.559\", \"0.247\", \"0.146\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: 5-signal AUROC comparison across NER full / RE full / RE cond. Structural signals (voting, SJ) consistently above logprob on NER but mixed on RE full.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Median 档 reviewer 的典型反应：'The logprob result on NER is expected — for structured outputs,\n      token-level log-probability doesn't capture set-level quality. This is not surprising.' \n      这直接命中核心假设 #1（novelty 受质疑）。但 SJ vs logprob delta 达到 0.217，数值上足够\n      striking 避免被完全 dismiss。RE full set 上 logprob 略胜的事实会被标记为 W1。\n\n  - name: \"baseline_exact_match\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-013\"\n    description: \"Exact-match voting rate as Wang et al. 2023 self-consistency baseline.\"\n    expected_results:\n      ner_full_rho: 0.294\n      ner_full_auroc: 0.640\n      re_full_rho: 0.156\n      re_full_auroc: 0.586\n    result_rationale: >\n      EM 处于 SJ 和 FK 之间（NER ρ=0.294），在 RE 上最弱（ρ=0.156）。这符合预期：exact match\n      对 structured outputs 过于粗粒度，一个 entity span 差异即判定为 mismatch。Median 档 reviewer\n      认为这是 'correct but unsurprising baseline'——Wang et al. 的 self-consistency 在\n      structured prediction 上不 work 是 intuitive 的。EM 的弱势反而支撑了引入 SJ 的动机，\n      但 reviewer 会指出这个动机本身不够 novel（'expected for structured outputs'）。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      EM 作为最直接的 self-consistency 迁移失败，证明 structured outputs 需要更精细的比较。\n      但 median reviewer 不会给这个发现太多 credit——它太 intuitive。\n\n  - name: \"baseline_entity_voting\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-014\"\n    description: \"Entity-level majority voting confidence and selection.\"\n    expected_results:\n      ner_full_rho: 0.392\n      ner_full_auroc: 0.704\n      re_full_rho: 0.340\n      re_full_auroc: 0.667\n      ner_voting_f1: 0.625\n      ner_greedy_f1: 0.648\n      re_voting_f1: 0.358\n      re_greedy_f1: 0.402\n    result_rationale: >\n      Voting confidence 在 NER 上 beats SJ（ρ 0.392 vs 0.383），在 RE 上也领先（0.340 vs 0.244）。\n      这对论文叙事产生压力：如果一个更简单的 entity-level voting 就够了，SJ 的价值在哪？\n      Median 档 reviewer 的 R3b 质疑被触发。但 voting 作为 selection strategy 输给 greedy\n      （NER 0.625 < 0.648），强化了 Claim 2 的 correlation-selection gap 叙事。\n      论文需要将 voting 和 SJ 定位为 'structural consistency family 的两个互补成员'：\n      voting 简单高效是实用默认，SJ 可推广到任意 structured output 且温度鲁棒（Δρ=±0.01）。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Voting 的出现实际上帮助了论文：它扩大了 structural consistency family 的覆盖面，\n      同时 voting-as-selection 的失败成为 Claim 2 的证据。Median reviewer 接受这个 framing\n      但可能仍嫌 '两个信号讲一个故事' 的贡献不够 novel。\n\n  - name: \"evaluation_metrics_expansion\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-015\"\n    description: \"Unified 5-signal evaluation: ρ, τ, AUROC, leave-one-out SJ on all datasets.\"\n    expected_results:\n      ner_voting_rho_full: 0.502\n      ner_voting_auroc: 0.728\n      ner_sj_rho_full: 0.357\n      ner_sj_auroc: 0.666\n      ner_logprob_auroc: 0.559\n      re_voting_rho_full: 0.422\n      re_voting_auroc: 0.716\n      re_sj_auroc: 0.582\n      re_logprob_auroc: 0.635\n      focal_auroc_gap_ner: 0.107\n      focal_auroc_gap_re: -0.053\n      loo_sj_max_delta_rho: 0.000305\n    result_rationale: >\n      Unified evaluation 使 NER 上 structural vs logprob 的 AUROC gap 达到 0.107（voting 0.728 vs logprob 0.559），\n      落在 median 档 focal_auroc_gap 范围 [0.05, 0.10] 的上沿。这是论文最强的数字之一。\n      但 RE full 上 SJ AUROC（0.582）低于 logprob（0.635），gap 为负。Median reviewer\n      会用这个数据点 argue 'signal superiority is dataset/task-dependent'。\n      Leave-one-out SJ 无循环性（max Δρ=0.0003），解决了 R9 circularity concern，\n      reviewer 会 acknowledge 这个 robustness check。τ 与 ρ 方向一致增强了 soundness。\n      整体 perceived_soundness 在 [3.0, 4.0] 范围——方法论扎实但结论受 RE 数据限制。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Unified Quality Estimation (SciERC, N=8, T=1.0)\"\n        columns: [\"Signal\", \"NER ρ\", \"NER τ\", \"NER AUROC\", \"RE ρ\", \"RE τ\", \"RE AUROC\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"voting_conf\", \"0.502\", \"0.377\", \"0.728\", \"0.422\", \"0.327\", \"0.716\"]\n          - [\"SJ\", \"0.357\", \"0.266\", \"0.666\", \"0.211\", \"0.162\", \"0.582\"]\n          - [\"FK\", \"0.265\", \"0.203\", \"0.624\", \"0.253\", \"0.197\", \"0.631\"]\n          - [\"EM\", \"0.257\", \"0.192\", \"0.623\", \"0.100\", \"0.084\", \"0.504\"]\n          - [\"logprob\", \"0.140\", \"0.101\", \"0.559\", \"0.247\", \"0.181\", \"0.635\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Reliability diagram (calibration): 5 signals × NER/RE. Shows voting well-calibrated on NER, all signals poorly calibrated on RE.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Unified evaluation 是论文 soundness 的基石。Median reviewer 给 soundness 3.5/5\n      因为方法论正确但 RE 数据不支持 universal claim。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Claim 1: Cross-Dataset / Cross-Model Generalization\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"ner_conll2003\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: \"Qwen3-8B on CoNLL-2003 NER. Cross-dataset generalization.\"\n    expected_results:\n      sj_rho_full: 0.436\n      sj_auroc_full: 0.801\n      fk_rho_full: 0.400\n      logprob_rho_full: 0.316\n      em_rho_full: 0.451\n      ev_rho_full: 0.424\n      greedy_f1: 0.912\n      oracle_f1: 0.954\n      oracle_headroom: 0.042\n      sj_vs_logprob_delta_rho: 0.120\n      n_valid: 2756\n    result_rationale: >\n      CoNLL 上 SJ ρ=0.436 高于 SciERC（0.357），因为 CoNLL 是简单 flat NER 任务，\n      模型 greedy F1 已达 0.912，consistency signal 更 reliable。SJ AUROC 0.801 是全实验最高值之一。\n      但 oracle headroom 仅 0.042（vs SciERC 0.108），意味着 best-of-N selection 的实用价值很小。\n      Median reviewer 接受 cross-dataset generalization 但注意到：(a) CoNLL 太容易，consistency\n      高是 trivial 的；(b) headroom 小说明 TTS 本身无意义。这强化了 'quality estimation, not selection'\n      的 framing 但也让 reviewer 问 'if the model is already 91% F1, who needs confidence estimation?'。\n      EM 在 CoNLL 上意外地最强（ρ=0.451），因为高准确率下 exact match 率足够区分 easy/hard。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: Cross-Dataset Quality Estimation (CoNLL-2003 NER)\"\n        columns: [\"Signal\", \"ρ\", \"τ\", \"AUROC\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"EM\", \"0.451\", \"0.400\", \"0.816\"]\n          - [\"SJ\", \"0.436\", \"0.385\", \"0.801\"]\n          - [\"voting_conf\", \"0.424\", \"0.378\", \"0.789\"]\n          - [\"FK\", \"0.400\", \"0.357\", \"0.774\"]\n          - [\"logprob\", \"0.316\", \"0.247\", \"0.753\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      CoNLL 数据 confirms structural > logprob cross-dataset，但 EM 抢占 SJ 位置\n      使 'SJ is best' 的 claim 需要 nuance。论文必须 argue SJ generalizability 而非 SJ dominance。\n\n  - name: \"ner_wnut17\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: \"WNUT-17 social media NER. Abandoned due to 54% F1=0.\"\n    expected_results:\n      sj_rho_full: 0.082\n      fk_rho_full: 0.124\n      logprob_rho_full: -0.414\n      sample_f1_pct_zero: 53.7\n      n_instances: 1287\n      verdict: FAIL\n    result_rationale: >\n      WNUT 失败是 median 档的重要 data point。54% 的 sample F1=0 意味着模型在 social media\n      domain 能力不足——consistency signal 在模型 systematically 失败时无意义。这既是\n      Claim 3（task-complexity boundary）的证据，也是 limitation：论文无法 claim generalization\n      到 noisy/informal text。Median reviewer 看到 WNUT 被 orphaned 会标记为 'only tested on\n      well-structured text domains'（R1 concern）。论文选择不报告 WNUT 在 Limitations 中\n      acknowledge，reviewer 认为 honest 但仍视为 scope 不足。Logprob 出现负相关（ρ=-0.414）\n      是因为模型对 noisy text 过度自信——生成流畅但错误的 output 有高 logprob。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      WNUT failure 不进入 main results 但作为 Claim 3 的 negative evidence 在 Discussion 中简述。\n      Median reviewer 不会因此 reject 但会在 scope concern 中引用。\n\n  - name: \"ner_multi_model\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: \"LLaMA-3.1-8B on SciERC. Model-agnostic validation.\"\n    expected_results:\n      ner_rho_sj: 0.363\n      ner_rho_fk: 0.327\n      ner_rho_logprob: 0.183\n      ner_sj_beats_surface: true\n      re_rho_sj: 0.299\n      re_rho_logprob: 0.288\n      re_sj_cond: 0.405\n      re_logprob_cond: 0.092\n      re_sample_f1_pct_zero: 41.2\n    result_rationale: >\n      LLaMA NER 上 SJ（0.363）> logprob（0.183），structural > surface 一致成立，\n      支撑 model-agnostic claim。但 RE full set 上 SJ（0.299）仅微弱领先 logprob（0.288），\n      且均 < 0.30。RE cond 上 SJ 大幅反弹（0.405），但 41.2% 的 RE sample F1=0 \n      表明 LLaMA 在 SciERC RE 上同样面临 capability gap。\n      Median reviewer 接受 2-model validation 但指出：'Both 8B models show similar patterns.\n      A 70B model or a fundamentally different architecture would strengthen the generalization claim.'\n      这触发 R14（cross-model validation thin），但不致命——reviewer 视为 P1 而非 P0 concern，\n      因为 2×8B across 2 architectures（Qwen/LLaMA）至少排除了 model-specific artifact。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 4: Cross-Model Validation (LLaMA-3.1-8B, SciERC)\"\n        columns: [\"Subtask\", \"Signal\", \"ρ full\", \"ρ cond\", \"AUROC\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"NER\", \"SJ\", \"0.363\", \"0.311\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"NER\", \"logprob\", \"0.183\", \"0.109\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"RE\", \"SJ\", \"0.299\", \"0.405\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"RE\", \"logprob\", \"0.288\", \"0.092\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Cross-model evidence 足够支撑 'model-agnostic' 在 softened form 下通过 review，\n      但 median reviewer 会在 major weakness 中写 'limited to 8B parameter scale'。\n\n  - name: \"ner_llama_conll\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-017\"\n    description: \"LLaMA-3.1-8B on CoNLL-2003 for 2×2 matrix completion.\"\n    expected_results:\n      sj_rho_full: 0.431\n      fk_rho_full: 0.428\n      logprob_rho_full: 0.307\n      voting_conf_rho_full: 0.426\n      sj_auroc_full: 0.704\n      logprob_auroc_full: 0.761\n      greedy_f1: 0.927\n      n_valid: 2756\n    result_rationale: >\n      LLaMA×CoNLL 完成 2×2 矩阵（Qwen×LLaMA × SciERC×CoNLL）。SJ ρ=0.431 与 Qwen×CoNLL\n      的 0.436 高度一致，证明 cross-model consistency。这是论文 generalization 最强论据。\n      但 AUROC 上 logprob（0.761）反超 SJ（0.704）——CoNLL 高准确率场景下 logprob\n      的 discriminative power 更强。Median reviewer 注意到 AUROC ranking 与 ρ ranking 不一致\n      （SJ wins ρ, logprob wins AUROC on CoNLL），这会引发 'which metric matters more?' 的讨论。\n      论文需要 argue ρ 更 informative 因为它测量 monotonic ordering 而非 binary discrimination。\n      cross_config_ner_structural_gt_logprob_rate 在 ρ 上为 4/4（100%），在 AUROC 上为 2/4（50%），\n      落在 median 档 [0.8, 1.0] 的边缘——取决于论文主推哪个 metric。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: 2×2 Cross-Validation Matrix (NER ρ full)\"\n        columns: [\"\", \"SciERC\", \"CoNLL-2003\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Qwen3-8B\", \"0.357 (SJ) / 0.140 (lp)\", \"0.436 (SJ) / 0.316 (lp)\"]\n          - [\"LLaMA-3.1-8B\", \"0.363 (SJ) / 0.183 (lp)\", \"0.431 (SJ) / 0.307 (lp)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: 2×2 matrix showing SJ ρ across model×dataset. All cells > 0.35, all structural > logprob.\"\n    analysis: >\n      2×2 矩阵是 reviewer R1+R2 的核心回应。4/4 configurations 上 structural ρ > logprob ρ。\n      Median reviewer 认可但注意到都是 8B 规模和 well-structured text，scope concern 不消。\n\n  - name: \"ner_n16_scierc\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: \"N=16 with 3-seed robustness on SciERC.\"\n    expected_results:\n      ner_sj_rho_mean_3seed: 0.412\n      ner_sj_rho_sd_3seed: 0.025\n      ner_voting_conf_rho_s42: 0.399\n      ner_sj_rho_s42: 0.398\n      re_sj_rho_s42: 0.277\n      re_voting_conf_rho_s42: 0.380\n      re_full_verdict: FAIL\n    result_rationale: >\n      3-seed NER SJ ρ 均值 0.412（SD=0.025），稳定性良好。N=16 vs N=8 在 NER 上\n      marginal improvement（0.412 vs 0.357），说明 N=8 已接近饱和。RE full set SJ ρ=0.277 \n      仍远低于 0.40 阈值，N=16 未能挽救 RE。这是 median 档的关键数据：\n      reviewer 看到 RE rho < 0.30 会 argue 'consistency signals fundamentally limited for \n      relational tasks'，将 Claim 1 的适用范围限制在 NER。论文通过 conditional analysis\n      部分挽回（RE cond SJ ρ~0.37-0.40），但这只占 2/3 的实例。\n      3-seed 稳定性是正面信号——soundness 得分因此在 3.5 左右而非更低。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 6: N-Scaling & Seed Robustness (SciERC)\"\n        columns: [\"Config\", \"NER SJ ρ\", \"RE SJ ρ\", \"NER AUROC\", \"RE AUROC\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"N=8, s42\", \"0.383\", \"0.244\", \"0.689\", \"0.592\"]\n          - [\"N=16, s42\", \"0.398\", \"0.277\", \"0.697\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"N=16, s123\", \"0.423\", \"0.267\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"N=16, s456\", \"0.414\", \"0.268\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"N=16 mean±SD\", \"0.412±0.025\", \"0.271±0.006\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Seed stability 强（SD=0.025），RE 一致地弱（3 seed 均 < 0.28）。\n      Median reviewer：'The authors appropriately report multi-seed results. RE weakness \n      is a real limitation, not a statistical artifact.'\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Claim 2: Correlation-Selection Gap\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"adaptive_compute_demo\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: \"Best-of-N selection: all signals vs greedy vs oracle.\"\n    expected_results:\n      ner_scierc_greedy: 0.618\n      ner_scierc_sj: 0.620\n      ner_scierc_logprob: 0.621\n      ner_scierc_oracle: 0.787\n      ner_conll_greedy: 0.725\n      ner_conll_sj: 0.718\n      re_greedy: 0.403\n      re_logprob: 0.410\n      re_sj: 0.397\n      re_oracle: 0.631\n    result_rationale: >\n      NER best-of-N：所有信号 ≤ greedy（SJ 0.620 ≈ greedy 0.618，差异 statistically insignificant），\n      oracle headroom +16.9pp 完全无法 exploit。这是 Claim 2 的核心负面发现。\n      RE：仅 logprob（0.410）beat greedy（0.403，+0.7pp），SJ（0.397）反而略低于 greedy。\n      Median reviewer 的反应两极：一方面 'negative result is interesting and honest'，\n      另一方面 'if your signals can't improve anything, what's the practical value?'。\n      NER selection 全面失败在 median 档被至少 1 位 reviewer 视为 significant limitation（核心假设 #6）。\n      论文必须 pivot 叙事：'These results reveal a fundamental gap between quality estimation \n      (knowing which INPUTS are reliable) and sample selection (choosing which OUTPUT is best).'\n      Oracle gap 的存在（NER +16pp, RE +23pp）说明 better signals 理论上可行——current unsupervised \n      signals 还不够。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 7: Best-of-N Selection F1 (SciERC, N=16)\"\n        columns: [\"Signal\", \"NER F1\", \"Δ vs greedy\", \"RE F1\", \"Δ vs greedy\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"greedy\", \"0.618\", \"—\", \"0.403\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"logprob\", \"0.621\", \"+0.003\", \"0.410\", \"+0.007\"]\n          - [\"SJ\", \"0.620\", \"+0.002\", \"0.397\", \"−0.006\"]\n          - [\"FK\", \"0.621\", \"+0.003\", \"0.396\", \"−0.007\"]\n          - [\"voting_conf\", \"0.585\", \"−0.033\", \"0.408\", \"+0.005\"]\n          - [\"random\", \"0.586\", \"−0.032\", \"0.364\", \"−0.039\"]\n          - [\"oracle\", \"0.787\", \"+0.169\", \"0.631\", \"+0.228\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 1 (KEY FIGURE): Selection curves — F1 vs N (1,2,4,8,16) for each signal + oracle + greedy baseline. NER: all signals flat at greedy level, oracle soars. RE: logprob slightly rises, others flat. Visually dramatic gap between oracle ceiling and signal performance.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Selection curves figure 是论文最重要的 visualization——它让 correlation-selection gap \n      一目了然。Median reviewer 评价 Claim 2 为 'interesting observation but unclear practical impact'\n      （核心假设 #2）。需要 actionable guidance 回应 'so what'。\n\n  - name: \"signal_ensemble_analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-016\"\n    description: \"SJ+logprob ensemble, linear combination grid search, logistic regression.\"\n    expected_results:\n      sj_logprob_pearson_ner: 0.57\n      sj_logprob_pearson_re: 0.42\n      best_linear_ner_combo: \"SJ+voting_conf α=0.3\"\n      best_linear_ner_rho: 0.489\n      best_linear_re_combo: \"voting_conf+logprob α=0.6\"\n      best_linear_re_rho: 0.429\n      ensemble_ner_auroc: 0.735\n      ensemble_re_auroc: 0.719\n      ensemble_ner_delta_auroc: 0.035\n      selection_ner_ensemble_f1: 0.604\n      selection_ner_greedy_f1: 0.609\n      selection_re_logprob_f1: 0.397\n      selection_re_greedy_f1: 0.374\n    result_rationale: >\n      Ensemble NER AUROC 0.735 比 best single 0.700 提升 +0.035——improvement 存在但 marginal。\n      RE ensemble AUROC 0.719 实际略低于 voting_conf 单独的 0.721，无 improvement。\n      SJ 和 logprob 的 Pearson 相关 0.57 说明二者 moderately correlated——它们捕获的信息\n      有 overlap 也有 complement。Linear combo 最佳组合是 SJ+voting（NER）和 voting+logprob（RE），\n      而非 SJ+logprob——这暗示同 family 内组合（structural×structural）比跨 family 更有效。\n      关键 negative：ensemble 也无法 beat greedy on NER selection（0.604 < 0.609）。\n      Median reviewer 认为 ensemble 分析 comprehensive 但 '强化了 negative result 而非解决它'。\n      Effective claim count = 2（quality estimation + gap），ensemble 是 supporting evidence 不是独立 claim。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: Ensemble Analysis\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"NER ρ\", \"NER AUROC\", \"RE ρ\", \"RE AUROC\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Best single (voting_conf)\", \"0.502\", \"0.728\", \"0.422\", \"0.716\"]\n          - [\"Best linear combo\", \"0.489\", \"—\", \"0.429\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Logistic regression ensemble\", \"—\", \"0.735\", \"—\", \"0.719\"]\n          - [\"Oracle\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Ensemble 结果 resolves R11 但不改变 paper narrative。\n      Median reviewer 给 credit for thoroughness，不 penalize。\n\n  - name: \"selection_curves\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-010\"\n    description: \"Best-of-N curves for N=1,2,4,8,16 across all datasets.\"\n    expected_results:\n      scierc_ner_n16_oracle: 0.787\n      scierc_ner_n16_best_signal: 0.621\n      scierc_ner_n4_oracle: 0.714\n      scierc_re_n16_logprob: 0.410\n      scierc_re_n8_logprob: 0.413\n      conll_ner_n8_sj: 0.718\n      conll_ner_n8_greedy: 0.725\n    result_rationale: >\n      Selection curves 跨 N 值的 pattern 高度一致：NER 上所有信号 flat at greedy level，\n      RE 上仅 logprob 微幅超越。CoNLL NER 上 N=8 所有信号（SJ 0.718）反而低于 greedy（0.725），\n      因为 CoNLL 高准确率下 T=1.0 的 stochastic samples 引入 noise 而非 diversity。\n      Oracle 随 N 单调增长（NER: 0.714→0.787），说明 sample pool 中确实存在更好 output，\n      但 unsupervised signals 无法识别。这个 gap 的视觉化（Figure 1）是论文最有 impact 的贡献。\n      Median reviewer 认为这个 figure 比任何 table 更 convincing，但仍可能 comment \n      'the gap is well-documented but the authors offer no path forward'。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 1: Selection curves (described in exp-006). Includes all 3 datasets × NER + SciERC RE. 12 subplots, each showing F1 vs N with confidence band.\"\n    analysis: >\n      这个 figure 直接回应 R16（zero figures），是 median 档论文从 table-only 升级的关键。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Claim 3: Task-Complexity Boundary\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"re_diagnostic_analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: \"Per-relation-type breakdown, error propagation, threshold sensitivity, bootstrap CI.\"\n    expected_results:\n      hyponym_rho_sj: 0.545\n      feature_of_rho_sj: 0.004\n      used_for_rho_sj: 0.236\n      entity_span_error_pct: 55.5\n      fisher_z_ner_vs_re_sj_p: 0.021\n      bootstrap_ci_ner_sj: [0.295, 0.459]\n      bootstrap_ci_re_sj: [0.142, 0.339]\n      threshold_thr0_rho_sj: 0.316\n      threshold_thr0_n: 313\n    result_rationale: >\n      Per-relation analysis 揭示巨大异质性：HYPONYM-OF ρ_sj=0.545（接近 NER 水平），\n      FEATURE-OF ρ_sj=0.004（近乎零）。这种 within-task variance 比 NER-vs-RE 的 between-task\n      差异更有 diagnostic value。Entity span errors 占 RE FN 的 55.5%，说明 RE failure\n      主要是 entity 识别失败导致的 cascade——compound error propagation 实锤。\n      Fisher Z-test 确认 NER ρ_sj significantly > RE ρ_sj（p=0.021）。\n      Median reviewer 视这些为 'solid descriptive analysis' 但不是 'prescriptive framework'\n      （R17 concern）。Bootstrap CI 显示 NER SJ 和 RE SJ 的 95% CI 有 overlap（NER [0.295, 0.459] \n      vs RE [0.142, 0.339]）——虽然均值差异显著但不是 dramatic separation。\n      Threshold sensitivity 分析显示 thr=0.00 时 ρ=0.316（n=313），thr=0.05 时 ρ 反降至 0.268（n=239），\n      说明 conditional threshold 不是 monotonically beneficial——只是 F1=0 的 extreme cases 拉低了相关。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: Per-Relation-Type Quality Estimation (SciERC RE)\"\n        columns: [\"Relation Type\", \"n\", \"ρ_SJ\", \"ρ_FK\", \"ρ_VC\", \"Mean F1\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"HYPONYM-OF\", \"36\", \"0.545\", \"0.646\", \"0.628\", \"0.513\"]\n          - [\"CONJUNCTION\", \"86\", \"0.383\", \"0.350\", \"0.484\", \"0.480\"]\n          - [\"USED-FOR\", \"299\", \"0.236\", \"0.255\", \"0.286\", \"0.422\"]\n          - [\"PART-OF\", \"44\", \"0.239\", \"0.348\", \"0.283\", \"0.297\"]\n          - [\"EVALUATE-FOR\", \"62\", \"0.172\", \"0.255\", \"0.226\", \"0.365\"]\n          - [\"COMPARE\", \"35\", \"0.168\", \"0.184\", \"0.180\", \"0.453\"]\n          - [\"FEATURE-OF\", \"50\", \"0.004\", \"0.052\", \"0.014\", \"0.254\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 2: Error propagation decomposition — stacked bar chart showing RE FN by error source (head span, tail span, type, head+tail). Entity span errors dominate.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Diagnostic analysis 最强贡献是 error decomposition 和 per-relation heterogeneity。\n      Median reviewer 接受这些但要求 soften 'diagnostic framework' → 'empirical analysis'。\n\n  - name: \"temperature_sensitivity_analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: \"T=0.7 vs T=1.0 comparison for all signals.\"\n    expected_results:\n      sj_delta_rho_t07_vs_t10: 0.01\n      fk_delta_rho_t07_vs_t10: 0.06\n      recommendation: \"T=1.0 + conditional filtering\"\n      re_oracle_headroom_t10: 0.167\n      re_oracle_headroom_t07: 0.131\n      re_diversity_1_sj_t10: 0.389\n      re_diversity_1_sj_t07: 0.313\n    result_rationale: >\n      SJ 温度鲁棒性极强（Δρ=±0.01 across T=0.7/1.0），FK 受温度影响更大（Δρ=±0.06-0.09）。\n      这是 SJ 相对于 FK 的独特优势之一，在 R3b 的回应中有价值。\n      T=1.0 保留更多 oracle headroom（RE: 0.167 vs 0.131）和多样性（1-SJ: 0.389 vs 0.313），\n      但 selection 上无 signal 能 exploit 这个 headroom。\n      Conditional filtering 的 lift（+0.07~0.14）远大于温度调优（±0.01），\n      说明 '智能过滤 > 参数调优' 是一个 practical recommendation。\n      Median reviewer 认为温度分析 'adequate but not a standalone contribution'。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      温度分析作为 Claim 3 的 supporting evidence，不独立贡献 novelty。\n      SJ 的温度鲁棒性是 reviewer 质疑 R3b 时的防御点。\n\n  - name: \"capability_stratification\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: \"Instance stratification by difficulty and independent proxies.\"\n    expected_results:\n      ner_sj_rho_overall: 0.398\n      ner_by_ent_count_0_sj_rho: 0.689\n      ner_by_ent_count_3_5_sj_rho: 0.353\n      re_hard_0_25_sj_rho: -0.043\n      re_easy_sj_rho: 0.210\n      inverted_u_confirmed: false\n      proxy_independence_ner_f1_vs_slen: -0.021\n    result_rationale: >\n      Entity count=0 时 SJ ρ=0.689（最高），因为空实例的 binary judgment 更清晰。\n      RE hard instances（greedy F1 < 0.25）SJ ρ=-0.043（近乎随机），证明 consistency signal\n      在模型 capability 之外完全失效。Inverted-U pattern 未确认——这是 honest negative \n      但也意味着论文不能 claim 'sweet spot' 的存在。Independent proxy（句长、entity count）\n      与 F1 几乎正交（r=-0.021, 0.007），验证了分层不是 circular。\n      Median reviewer 视为 solid analysis 但 'descriptive, not actionable'：\n      知道 hard instances 的 signal 弱不能帮助 practitioner 决定何时 trust。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 3: Scatter plot — instance SJ vs F1, colored by difficulty stratum. Shows signal collapse in hard-RE region (bottom-left cluster).\"\n    analysis: >\n      Stratification 支撑 Claim 3 但 inverted-U 不确认意味着 'complexity boundary' \n      是 monotonic degradation 而非 non-linear pattern。叙事需对应调整。\n\n  - name: \"re_n16_confirmation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: \"RE N=16 on SciERC — test N-scaling effect on RE.\"\n    expected_results:\n      re_rho_sj_full: 0.297\n      re_rho_sj_cond: 0.398\n      re_rho_logprob_full: 0.299\n      re_headroom: 0.232\n      ner_rho_sj_full: 0.377\n      verdict: FAIL\n    result_rationale: >\n      N=16 对 RE 的改善 marginal：SJ ρ 从 N=8 的 0.211 升至 0.297（+0.086），\n      仍远低于 0.40。Logprob 在 N=16 上 ρ=0.299 与 SJ 几乎相同——更多 samples 缩小了\n      SJ 和 logprob 的差距但都没超越 0.30 barrier。Headroom 扩大到 0.232，\n      但 signal 改善幅度远不够 exploit。Conditional set ρ_sj=0.398 接近 0.40 阈值\n      但仍 borderline。这确认了 RE consistency signal 的弱势不是 sample budget 问题——\n      即使 N=16 也不够。早期在 200 instance subset + T=0.7 上观察到的 N-scaling 'breakthrough'\n      被证实是 artifact（核心假设 #5：RE ρ < 0.30 限制 claim scope）。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      RE N=16 的 FAIL verdict 是论文最大的 inconvenient truth。\n      Median reviewer：'Even with doubled compute budget, RE quality estimation remains weak.'\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Remaining / Planned\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"ner_ood_robustness\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-011\"\n    description: \"NER OOD robustness via cross-domain transfer (e.g., SciERC model on CoNLL or vice versa).\"\n    expected_results:\n      ood_sj_rho_full: 0.15\n      ood_fk_rho_full: 0.10\n      ood_logprob_rho_full: -0.20\n      ood_sample_f1_pct_zero: 35.0\n      ood_greedy_f1: 0.45\n      structural_beats_surface: true\n      verdict: MARGINAL\n    result_rationale: >\n      OOD 场景下模型 greedy F1 大幅下降（~0.45 vs in-domain 0.66），consistency signal \n      相应退化但 structural 仍优于 surface（SJ ρ~0.15 > FK ρ~0.10）。Logprob 在 OOD 下\n      出现负相关（ρ~-0.20），因为 domain shift 导致 logprob 与 accuracy 脱钩——模型\n      对 in-domain-like patterns 过度自信。这是 SJ 在 closed-source API / OOD 场景下\n      独特价值的支撑：即使绝对 ρ 不高，至少 direction 正确且不会 mislead。\n      35% F1=0 rate 类似 WNUT，说明 OOD performance 受模型 capability 限制。\n      Median reviewer 不会 heavily weight 这个实验（P2），但它回应了 R18（when would \n      consistency help?）——answer：当 logprob 不可用或不可信时。\n      注意：这是唯一 truly unrun 的 planned 实验，预测有更大不确定性。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table (Appendix): OOD Robustness\"\n        columns: [\"Signal\", \"In-Domain ρ\", \"OOD ρ\", \"Δ\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"SJ\", \"0.357\", \"0.15\", \"−0.207\"]\n          - [\"FK\", \"0.265\", \"0.10\", \"−0.165\"]\n          - [\"logprob\", \"0.140\", \"−0.20\", \"−0.340\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      OOD 实验如果执行会进入 Appendix 而非 main results。Median reviewer 不太可能\n      要求这个实验作为 acceptance condition，但它回应了 closed-source API applicability 叙事。\n      实际执行风险：如果 OOD F1 太低（<0.30），consistency analysis 失去意义。\n      建议：如果 GPU 时间允许，仅作为 supplementary evidence，不影响 main claims。\n```\n\n**关键 median-tier 总结**：\n\n- **effective_claim_count_accepted = 2**：Claim 1（quality estimation taxonomy）和 Claim 2（correlation-selection gap）被接受；Claim 3 弱化为 descriptive analysis 不算独立贡献\n- **focal_auroc_gap**：NER 上 0.107（voting vs logprob），在 [0.05, 0.10] 上沿，足够 striking；RE 上为负，限制 universal claim\n- **cross_config rate**：ρ metric 上 4/4 = 100%，AUROC 上仅 2/4 = 50%，论文需主推 ρ\n- **RE full ρ_sj < 0.30** 跨所有 config 一致成立，是 median 档最大 scope limitation\n- **NER selection failure**（all ≤ greedy）被 1 位 reviewer 视为 significant limitation，但 correlation-selection gap framing 将其转化为 finding","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"529d87e7-4ace-46b9-b80b-7e8c13d80a89","total_cost_usd":0.6777302500000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":40587,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":15299,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":40587,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":15299,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":40587,"cache_cr